# Generated from: specs/486-stop-frontmatter-fix-from-flagging-specs-whose-prose-mentions-issues/requirements.md
Feature: frontmatter-fix ignores prose Issues and preserves gherkin comment headers

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: AC1 prose "Issues" does not trigger frontmatter-fix
    Given a specs/404-restrict-drafted-issues-and-specs package with singular "**Issue**: #404"
    And its requirements heading is "# Requirements: Restrict Drafted Issues and Specs"
    When upgrade detection runs
    Then no frontmatter-fix item is reported for that package

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: AC2 a plural Issues field still triggers frontmatter-fix
    Given a specs/7-x package whose requirements.md has "**Issues**: #7, #9"
    When upgrade detection runs
    Then a frontmatter-fix item is reported for specs/7-x with primaryN 7

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: AC3 gherkin comment headers are updated in place without duplicates
    Given a feature.gherkin header "# Issues: #7, #9", "# Date: 2026-01-01", "# Status: Planning", "# Author: NMG"
    When an approved frontmatter-fix applies with target #7 and status Draft
    Then the header is "# Issue: #7", "# Date: 2026-01-01", "# Status: Draft", "# Author: NMG"
    And the file contains no bold Issue, Date, Status, or Author lines

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: AC4 bold-form frontmatter behavior is preserved
    Given spec files with "**Issues**: #7, #9" and "**Status**: Planning"
    When an approved frontmatter-fix applies
    Then the files contain "**Issue**: #7" and "**Status**: Draft" and are otherwise unchanged
